{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"# Cloud ADF codec — make the existing ADF encode Markdown-aware (bidirectional)\n\n## Context / Problem\nJira Cloud stores rich text as ADF (structured JSON). The reconciler **already\nemits ADF** on the Cloud outbound path — it does not push a plain-Markdown\nstring. The `RichTextCodec` seam (epic `e369`, story J3 / `aac8-…`) routes every\nCloud rich-text field through `AdfCodec`\n(`adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py`), a pass-through wrapper over the pinned\n`adapters/jira/adf.py`.\n\nThe real gap is that `adf.py`'s encode is **plain-text-structured, not\nMarkdown-aware**: `text_to_adf` (`adf.py:275`) splits the body into blocks on\nblank lines and emits each as a single `paragraph` node, rejoining soft-wrapped\nprose. Markdown block syntax (`##` headings, `-`/`1.` lists, ```` ``` ```` fences)\nand inline syntax (`**bold**`, `~~strike~~`, `[text](url)`) are carried as\n**literal characters inside paragraph text nodes**, so Cloud renders the raw\nMarkdown source instead of rich text. Decode (`adf_to_text`, `adf.py:26`) is\nADF→**plain text**. So the round trip is faithful only for plain prose; authored\nstructure is lost on display.\n\nThis story closes that gap: make the encode/decode **Markdown-aware** so Cloud\nrenders headings/lists/code/emphasis as native ADF and a fetched ADF body decodes\nback to the same Markdown — truly bidirectional — **behind the existing\n`AdfCodec` seam**, adding no new plumbing.\n\n## Prior art in this repo (the seam we build on — NOT greenfield)\n- `RichTextCodec` **Protocol** — `adapters/jira_family/rich_text.py`. Four ops:\n  `fit_outbound`, `normalize_outbound` (\"render as it reads after a round trip\"),\n  `to_wire`, `decode_inbound`. Owns all Jira-family rich-text conversion.\n- `AdfCodec` (Cloud) — `adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py`. Delegates each op to\n  `adf.py`; a test (`test_rich_text_codec.py::test_adf_codec_is_a_pass_through_to_the_pinned_adf_module`)\n  pins it as a wrapper, not a second copy. Lives on the Cloud side because ADR 0035\n  forbids `jira_family/` importing `adf.py`.\n- `adf.py` — `text_to_adf` (`:275`), `adf_to_text` (`:26`), `normalize_description`\n  (`:310` = `adf_to_text(text_to_adf(text))`, the send/diff fixed point),\n  `fit_text_to_adf_limit` (`:341`). Stdlib-only, ADF v3 node vocabulary already\n  present.\n- `OutboundFieldMapper` (`adapters/jira_family/outbound_mapper.py`) composes\n  `normalize_outbound(fit_outbound(value))` — the description convergence contract\n  we must preserve.\n- `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` (`:134`) — **SHARED plain-text** decode\n  (ticket 21ca). It is NOT this codec: it serves `inbound_translate._normalize_adf_body`\n  (inbound apply defense) AND `outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body` (comment\n  diff). It stays plain-text and behavior-compatible — see Scope guard.\n\n## Approach\n1. **Extend `adf.py` to be Markdown-aware, keeping `AdfCodec` a pass-through.**\n   Add `markdown_to_adf` / `adf_to_markdown` and repoint `AdfCodec.to_wire`,\n   `AdfCodec.decode_inbound`, and `AdfCodec.normalize_outbound` at them. The\n   existing plain `adf_to_text` stays for the shared `normalize_rich_text` callers\n   (blast radius contained to `AdfCodec`).\n2. **Conversion engine — vendored `marklas` (default), extend-`adf.py` weighed.**\n   A hand-rolled mistune converter ceilinged at 90.7% corpus fixed point (emphasis\n   serialization is the hard part); `adf.py` already carries the ADF node\n   vocabulary but only a plain-text encode. We adopt `marklas` (pure-Python,\n   mistune-based, MIT) for Markdown↔ADF because it clears the fixed-point rate the\n   hand-rolled path could not. **Default to a VENDORED copy under\n   `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` with the upstream sha recorded** (single-maintainer\n   bus-factor mitigated by vendoring, not a floating dependency); an optional\n   `pyproject` extra is a fallback only if vendoring proves impractical.\n   marklas's asserted capability is **not trusted blindly** — it is proven by the\n   corpus AC below; if it fails, we fall back to extending `adf.py`'s handlers\n   in-house.\n3. **Loop prevention — reuse the existing fixed-point model.** Keep\n   `normalize_outbound` as the \"reads-after-round-trip\" idempotent transform\n   (now `adf_to_markdown(markdown_to_adf(text))`), applied to both sides before the\n   description diff — the same convergence contract `OutboundFieldMapper` already\n   relies on. Fix the one true 2-cycle oscillator — co-located `strong`+`strikethrough`\n   (`**~~x~~**` ⇄ `~~**x~~**`, no canonical mark order) — with a deterministic\n   mark-order canonicalizer inside the codec, applied to both sides. The ~18\n   transient whitespace canonicalizations converge under normalize-both-sides.\n4. **Failure path (no silent data loss).** On any conversion error for a field,\n   log the ticket/body id and **fall back to the current plain-text ADF encode\n   (`adf.text_to_adf`) for that field** rather than aborting the reconcile.\n\n## Scope\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/adf.py` — add Markdown-aware\n  `markdown_to_adf`/`adf_to_markdown` (+ strikethrough/mark handling); keep plain\n  `adf_to_text` for shared callers.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/adapters/jira/rich_text_codec.py` — repoint\n  `AdfCodec.to_wire`/`decode_inbound`/`normalize_outbound` at the Markdown-aware\n  functions + mark-order canonicalizer.\n- `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` — vendored, sha-pinned upstream copy.\n- `pyproject.toml` — record the vendored sha (optional extra only as fallback).\n- **Guard:** `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` is intentionally NOT changed;\n  it stays plain-text so `inbound_translate._normalize_adf_body` and\n  `outbound_comments._normalize_comment_body` are unaffected.\n- `tests/` — corpus idempotence, mark-order, failure-path, live cutover.\n\n## Testing\n- **Structured round trip:** a body with a heading, a checklist, inline code, and\n  a link round-trips MD→ADF→MD to a fixed point (`test_cloud_adf_roundtrip`).\n- **Oscillation regression:** the two known combined strong+strikethrough bodies\n  converge in ≤1 pass after canonicalization; a permutation property test asserts\n  100% convergence.\n- **Corpus idempotence (verifies marklas):** over the 5,568 historical bodies,\n  MD→ADF→MD is a fixed point for ≥99.6%, residual whitespace-only-transient\n  (`test_cloud_corpus_idempotence`). This is the check that the external\n  capability is real; a miss triggers the adf.py-extension fallback.\n- **Failure path:** an un-convertible body falls back to plain-text ADF and the\n  reconcile does not abort (`test_cloud_adf_conversion_fallback`).\n- **Live cutover:** posting a converted ADF description to a live/staging Cloud\n  issue succeeds and renders as rich text (not literal source), asserted against\n  the Cloud characterization oracle (story J1, `acb2-…`) — `test_cloud_adf_live`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] `marklas` is vendored under `src/rebar/_vendor/marklas/` with the upstream\n  sha recorded in `pyproject.toml`; verified by an import test that asserts the\n  pinned sha.\n- [ ] `AdfCodec.to_wire` emits Markdown-aware ADF (heading/list/code/emphasis\n  nodes, not literal `#`/`-`/`**` text); verified by `test_cloud_adf_roundtrip`\n  asserting the ADF node types.\n- [ ] `AdfCodec.decode_inbound` decodes ADF→Markdown; verified by the same test\n  asserting the decoded Markdown equals the source.\n- [ ] The shared `inbound_fields.normalize_rich_text` still returns plain text\n  (unchanged behavior); verified by its existing tests remaining green.\n- [ ] The combined strong+strikethrough oscillation is eliminated by the\n  mark-order canonicalizer; verified by a regression test on the two known bodies\n  plus a permutation property test (100% convergence).\n- [ ] MD→ADF→MD is a fixed point for ≥99.6% of the 5,568 historical bodies, the\n  residual whitespace-only; verified by `test_cloud_corpus_idempotence`.\n- [ ] A conversion failure falls back to the plain-text ADF encode and does not\n  abort the reconcile; verified by `test_cloud_adf_conversion_fallback`.\n- [ ] A converted ADF description posted to a live/staging Cloud issue renders as\n  rich text; verified by `test_cloud_adf_live` against the J1 oracle."}},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1785804500951454001,"uuid":"edf16813-2c11-4b07-b217-93285f2bfbf8"}